 "subject": "Cannot install R packages on a mac",
 "messages_listed": 5,
 "last_activity": "2016-12-14T00:06:35Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "UxLgTs8_EAAJ",
   "from": "Jeff Adler",
   "author": "9b878c4039854482",
   "date": "2016-12-12T21:31:44Z",
   "subject": "Cannot install R packages on a mac",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Whenever I try to install packages on R on a mac (note: macOS Sierra, Version 10.12), I get the following error message (this happens with any package I attempt to install):</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>&gt; install.packages(&quot;dplyr&quot;, &quot;XML&quot;, &quot;xml2&quot;, &quot;rChoiceDialogs&quot;, &quot;stringi&quot;, &quot;stringr&quot;, &quot;gsubfn&quot;, &quot;stringdist&quot;, dependencies=TRUE)</div><div>Warning in install.packages(&quot;dplyr&quot;, &quot;XML&quot;, &quot;xml2&quot;, &quot;rChoiceDialogs&quot;, &quot;stringi&quot;,  :</div><div>  &#39;lib = &quot;XML&quot;&#39; is not writable</div><div>Would you like to use a personal library instead?  (y/n) y</div><div>Error in available[p1, dependencies, drop = FALSE] : </div><div>  incorrect number of dimensions</div><div>In addition: Warning message:</div><div>package ‘dplyr’ is not available (for R version 3.3.2) </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "gcbsKhhAEAAJ",
   "from": "Stefan Th. Gries",
   "author": "3edc58ee737edd94",
   "date": "2016-12-12T21:36:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: [CorpLing with R] Cannot install R packages on a mac",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\">Does that also happen when you start R with administrator rights? On Windows, you might want to right-click on R and choose &quot;<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">start R with administrator rights&quot;, on Linux, you might start R from the terminal with sudo R. Also, check the result of .libPaths() to see whether you have write access to those locations.</span></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "BXJhr3NBEAAJ",
